    "last_assistant_text": "The PoC triggered the crash. The output confirms:\n- SEGV at `TT_Get_MM_Var` line 2144 (`*c = FT_GET_LONG()`) — exactly the write through the corrupted coords pointer\n- Called from `setIntermediateAxis` → `LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput`\n- WRITE memory access at address 0x000000000003 (null page)\n\nThe vulnerability works as analyzed: adding a `CFF ` table to a TrueType variable font causes `sfnt_init_face` to zero `num_instances`, while `TT_Get_MM_Var` reads the original `fvar_head.instanceCount` from the table. The undersized allocation leads to out-of-bounds writes when iterating over the instance data, corrupting the `coords` pointer and crashing on the dereference.",
